message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "mfdfa-benchmark: a cross-implementation benchmark of DFA and MFDFA on EEG"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Samir
    family-names: Hossain
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8986-0946"
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Texas Tech University"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SamirHossain099/mfdfa-benchmark"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22547573
    description: "Concept DOI; resolves to the latest release"
keywords:
  - detrended fluctuation analysis
  - multifractal analysis
  - EEG
  - software reliability
  - reproducibility
  - scale invariance
abstract: >-
  Runs five open Python implementations of detrended fluctuation analysis and its
  multifractal extension over identical signals with one parameter grid: synthetic
  controls with analytically known exponents, controls carrying inserted constant runs,
  and two public EEG corpora. Includes an invariance test under rescaling of the input,
  a measurement of the segments discarded by an absolute variance threshold, the result
  tables behind every reported number, and the figure scripts.
